  path="/terms"
  heading="Terms"
  updated="20 August 2026"
>
  <p>
    Terms of use for this website. Engagement terms are a separate document and are agreed in
    writing before any work starts &#8212; nothing here creates a contract to do work.
  </p>

  <h2>The calculator is a model, not a measurement</h2>
  <p>
    The payback model on the homepage says so on its face, and it is worth repeating here. It
    projects a cumulative return per install from the assumptions you type into it. It is not
    connected to your app, it has never seen your data, and it does not know your actual retention.
  </p>
  <p>It assumes, among other things:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Geometric per-cycle retention &#8212; a constant renewal rate every billing cycle.</li>
    <li>Constant ARPDAU across tenure.</li>
    <li>No seasonality in eCPM.</li>
    <li>No organic uplift from paid spend.</li>
    <li>No involuntary-churn recovery.</li>
    <li>A steady state &#8212; no cohort-size or price changes over the horizon.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Real retention is not perfectly geometric: month one churns harder and then the curve flattens,
    which makes the model slightly pessimistic past month six. Do not commit a budget on the
    strength of it. It exists to show the shape of a problem &#8212; that a campaign can look dead
    at day 7 and be profitable at day 277 &#8212; not to price your media plan.
  </p>

  <h2>The figures in "Three findings"</h2>
  <p>
    Those are real findings from real audits, with client names withheld under the confidentiality
    terms of those engagements. They describe what we found in specific accounts. They are not a
    forecast of what we would find in yours, and they are not a promise of a result.
  </p>

  <h2>Contacting us</h2>
  <p>
    Send accurate information. The form goes to a person, and the more accurate it is, the more
    useful the reply. Do not send confidential material through it &#8212; it is a contact form, not
    a secure channel. If you need to share account access or data, we will agree how before you do.
  </p>
  <p>
    Sending an enquiry does not create a client relationship or any obligation on either side. We
    may decline work, and frequently do when the problem is not one we would improve.
  </p>

